# Input Handling Patterns

## Overview
CrossOver uses global input hooks via uiohook-napi for mouse and keyboard actions while the crosshair is active.

## Core Implementation
- [src/main/iohook.ts](mdc:src/main/iohook.ts) - Main input hook implementation
- [src/config/keys.ts](mdc:src/config/keys.ts) - Keycode mappings and constants
- [src/config/settings.ts](mdc:src/config/settings.ts) - Input behavior configuration

## Input Action Types

### 1. Follow Mouse
- Keeps crosshair centered on mouse cursor
- Uses `mousemove` events to update window position
- Enabled via `followMouseEnabled` setting

### 2. Secondary Actions
- Temporary crosshair modifications when bind is active
- Supports both keyboard keys and mouse buttons
- Two behaviors: `toggle` (press to toggle) or `hold` (active while held)

### 3. Tilt Actions
- Rotates crosshair by specified angle
- Separate binds for left tilt (negative angle) and right tilt (positive angle)
- Configurable tilt angle and behavior

## Event Handling Pattern

### Keyboard Events
```typescript
// Register keydown listener
uIOhook.on('keydown', (event: UiohookKeyboardEvent) => {
  if (event.keycode === trigger) {
    // Handle key press
  }
});

// Register keyup listener for hold behavior
uIOhook.on('keyup', (event: UiohookKeyboardEvent) => {
  if (event.keycode === trigger) {
    // Handle key release
  }
});
```

### Mouse Events
```typescript
// Mouse button events
uIOhook.on('mousedown', (event: UiohookMouseEvent) => {
  if (event.button === button) {
    // Handle mouse press
  }
});

uIOhook.on('mouseup', (event: UiohookMouseEvent) => {
  if (event.button === button) {
    // Handle mouse release
  }
});
```

## Behavior Types

### Toggle Behavior
- Single press toggles action on/off
- Subsequent presses reverse the state
- Used for persistent state changes

### Hold Behavior
- Action active only while key/button is held
- Automatically deactivates on release
- Used for temporary state changes

## Keycode Mapping
- [src/config/keys.ts](mdc:src/config/keys.ts) contains `iohookKeycodes` mapping
- Maps human-readable keys to numeric keycodes
- Maintains compatibility with original iohook keycodes

## State Management
- Actions update global state via [src/main/store-actions.ts](mdc:src/main/store-actions.ts)
- State changes trigger crosshair visual updates
- State persists across hook start/stop cycles

## Settings Integration
- Input settings managed in [src/renderer/components/pages/settings/general/SettingsActions.tsx](mdc:src/renderer/components/pages/settings/general/SettingsActions.tsx)
- Bind configuration uses [src/renderer/components/input/InputMouseKeyboardBind.tsx](mdc:src/renderer/components/input/InputMouseKeyboardBind.tsx)
- Settings types defined in [src/config/settings.ts](mdc:src/config/settings.ts)

## Security Considerations
- Input hooks require system accessibility permissions
- Hooks only active when crosshair window is open
- Graceful fallback when permissions denied
- Error handling prevents crashes from hook failures
